[sliver] These finite strips are the glyph strokes and 0.6 mm relief sides of the permanent integral disposal warning specified in hardware/markings/README.md. The warning uses 6.5 mm H capitals and its prescribed complete letter outlines. Their narrow visible faces implement that marking geometry; they are not remnants from intersecting enclosure clearance cutters. The recorded picks span the raised warning on the exterior rear wall. This raw face review establishes neither printed legibility nor support-contact quality.
alternatives: Widening every stroke to an ordinary structural-wall section changes glyph counters and text fit. Removing the glyphs removes the specified warning. A separate label or flush contrasting marking would replace the selected integral raised implementation and requires a product decision. Retain the marking’s actual outlines and assess any support contacts in its own production slice.
